<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Queue xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <fullName>GTM_Readout_Triage</fullName>
    <!-- The last step of GtmReadoutController.Generator.resolveOwnerId. A direct
         booking with no Engagement Link and no Opportunity has no rep to name,
         and GTM_Readout__c is Private, so a readout with no owner is a readout
         nobody can see. Before this queue existed the generator refused to
         create one at all, which meant those assessments quietly produced
         nothing. Now they land here for a human to claim.

         Named for what a rep sees in a list view and an owner picker, not for
         the code path that fills it.

         CASE. The review Case that Generator files against the readout follows
         the same owner, queue included, so an unclaimed readout and its review
         work sit in one place. Case is listed below and Task is not, and that
         asymmetry is the whole reason the Task was replaced: queue-owned Cases
         are a plain platform capability, whereas queue-owned Tasks additionally
         require the org preference Setup -> Activity Settings -> "Let users
         assign tasks to queues", which is org state this repo cannot deploy —
         so the old review Task silently failed to be created in exactly the
         case (nobody assigned) where it mattered most. -->
    <name>Unassigned Readouts</name>
    <doesSendEmailToMembers>false</doesSendEmailToMembers>
    <queueSobject>
        <sobjectType>Case</sobjectType>
    </queueSobject>
    <queueSobject>
        <sobjectType>GTM_Readout__c</sobjectType>
    </queueSobject>
</Queue>
